Experiment
    - Removed latent step length penalty, also penalized internal cot behavior by cutting format reward in half. Accuracy/format reward is 5:5 now, may change to 6:4 if results aren't impressive


2026/03/19
Current Situation
    - Reward hacking observed from previous experiment, additional changes need to be made

Experiment
    - Changed formatting to stricter answer checking, where format score is 0 if answer cannot be converted to an int/float
        - Incurs reward hacking by outputting any random number?
        - May have to increase accuracy reward ratio

Experiment2
    - After consulting Claude, I made the following modifications
        - Format-accuracy ration back to 2:8 (not from Claude)
        - KL divergence increased 0.001 -> 0.05 to increase regularization
            - clip ratio still kept to 10 to encourage exploration and allow large mode shifts
        - max_log_ratio clipped BEFORE torch.exp
        - ReduceLRonPlateau scheduler added to reduce LR every third eval steps if plateauing

Experiment3
    - Exp2 yielded severely bad results, so changed how negative reward is applied to iterations that did not produce a valid answer.
    - Used Claude to implement the following changes:
        - per-group normalized advantages instead of global normalized advantages
        - temperature in language sampling to complement dropout-induced different latent chains (MAY have to remove this)
        - FIX: now using eval mode when calculating loss & log-probs, to prevent different masks from creating different results

Experiment4
    - Upgraded to Opus for more accurate analysis, and reviewed past design changes
        - FIX: termination head now only attends to latent tokens, and not language tokens
        - removed language sampling, as it was causing massive noise in the mathematical calculations
            - May re-introduce termination sampling (not LM) again if results seem to be diverging

Experiment5
    - Regularization effect may be too strong, hindering training
        - reverted KL beta to 0.001

Experiment6
    - Claude made some okay-soudning suggestions:
        - KL beta at 0.01, clip ratio at 0.2 (since Deepseek-R1 was for a 60B model, and my model uses a sparser reward signal)
        - Termination head sampling is implemented for varied output

Next steps
    - If termination head proves unstable, may have to change experiment a bit by making the transformer essentially "predict" the correctness of the latent chain's results for each step
        - If prediction accuracy proves to be high, then could freeze the head and use it during the SFT phase of the model training.


